instruction.text:
The moderator has given you the floor for your opening statement. This is your first argument. NEVER narrate that the moderator has called on you. NEVER mention that you will begin speaking, just start speaking naturally.

Lead with the strongest evidence-grounded claim you can make about this topic: {{debate_headline}}

The core tension: {{conflict_description}}
The forced tradeoff: {{forced_tradeoff}}
What's actually at stake: {{decision_surface}}

State the mechanism -- how does your position actually produce the better outcome, step by step? Name the evidence tier you are working at. Establish the design question this debate must answer.

Be precise and direct. 30-60 seconds. After you make your point, stop speaking completely.
